#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99326a6d-a2e8-5c78-b743-2baf6f38e745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99326a6d-a2e8-5c78-b743-2baf6f38e745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717089} :answer-field/id #uuid "502f327b-0652-563a-b1f1-4d0bcf6e2df7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15229d08-6246-5357-ab3e-442bf9fde193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15229d08-6246-5357-ab3e-442bf9fde193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717081} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7ec3ad4-5c70-5a20-a56e-83e47d9f2607" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebdb6e80-ba37-5ba0-8ddd-0c19e48ed14e" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, starting at A(15, 0), moving clockwise.](images/fb/fbd5852fb6bf6a13f9f113442ec28347ad97d0924a4671e42ed6eef09b93aa14.png)\n\nThe circle shown is centered at $O(0,0)$ and passes through the labeled point $A$. Construct a set of parametric equations that traverse the circle once clockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The axis point is $A(15,0)$. Its distance from $O(0,0)$ is $15$, so the radius is $15$.\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, cosine is $1$ and sine is $0$. To start at $A(15,0)$, use cosine in the $x$-coordinate and sine in the $y$-coordinate. Choose the signs so that the next quarter-turn reaches $(0,-15)$, moving clockwise.\n\nThus the equations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=15\\cos\\theta\\\\\ny&=-15\\sin\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$ the point is $(15,0)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(0,-15)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $15$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee01ffa1-3042-5fc1-ab36-66faa1ed9142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee01ffa1-3042-5fc1-ab36-66faa1ed9142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717095} :answer-field/id #uuid "060a2e19-0d35-5704-98f8-4fd4dbdd7b26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a24c403-0c3d-5275-892e-a92c118a8fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a24c403-0c3d-5275-892e-a92c118a8fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717079} :answer-field/id #uuid "9172dab4-614d-54c4-b5b0-efadf27ed203" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f2a9d9d0-8435-5b89-b07b-3c1302f687bf" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, starting at A(20, 0), moving counterclockwise.](images/80/80c65d1f12cb7b212604b54bf17d5c007e702756e4cea6d43bab4a5f7ddb383d.png)\n\nThe circle shown is centered at $O(0,0)$ and passes through the labeled point $A$. Construct a set of parametric equations that traverse the circle once counterclockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The axis point is $A(20,0)$. Its distance from $O(0,0)$ is $20$, so the radius is $20$.\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, cosine is $1$ and sine is $0$. To start at $A(20,0)$, use cosine in the $x$-coordinate and sine in the $y$-coordinate. Choose the signs so that the next quarter-turn reaches $(0,20)$, moving counterclockwise.\n\nThus the equations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=20\\cos\\theta\\\\\ny&=20\\sin\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$ the point is $(20,0)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(0,20)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $20$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717104 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d8f259a-f71c-5a8f-a7f9-f753d2ed72b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717113} {:answer/id #uuid "825f9326-6607-50b7-b462-78d7c0925a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717115} {:answer/id #uuid "df410fc4-105a-521d-89e7-52cc11344586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=1296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717124} {:answer/id #uuid "f5faf0e0-b713-5bfd-a728-6d6d82ab765d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717129} {:answer/id #uuid "f89f860f-d835-58b2-a5e4-06bf301f3b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825f9326-6607-50b7-b462-78d7c0925a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717115} :answer-field/id #uuid "4366c4f3-0300-563a-a826-6716014c772c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "298b6859-5d6c-5500-b1d5-57afc14c5db6" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=6\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=6\\cos\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=6\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{1}{6}x&=\\sin\\theta \\\\ \ny&=6\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{1}{6}y&=\\cos\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{36}x^2&=\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{1}{36}y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $36$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{36}x^2+\\frac{1}{36}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{1}{36}\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=36$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $6$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100118e8-b934-5480-b5de-231edba9e97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{6561}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717100} {:answer/id #uuid "82cd9461-a733-519d-9391-f79df761eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717116} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9e5b53-f55f-5325-a055-0b4bb15f640c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717119} {:answer/id #uuid "e30f9080-286e-5c19-8e87-b3aee4fe1339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717126} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e4bf82-6cbc-5110-be9e-339e04ef0b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cd9461-a733-519d-9391-f79df761eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717116} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a32fe73-dacc-5a86-9140-393181424c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32b677f0-3c94-5f52-aca5-307dfa9bb6af" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{9}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{9}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{9}{2}\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{9}x&=\\sin\\theta \\\\ \ny&=\\frac{9}{2}\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{9}y&=\\cos\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{81}x^2&=\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{81}y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $\\frac{81}{4}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{81}x^2+\\frac{4}{81}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{81}\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{81}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{9}{2}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0091ca2a-4e0b-5a18-84fc-4e9a6bf310d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717098} {:answer/id #uuid "10d62fd6-731f-5adb-b8a5-2b89541312e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717101} {:answer/id #uuid "1c906f38-8816-5e95-b7e9-527436e068ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717103} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff8b912-fc25-51c6-abfb-2b5a13372f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717109} {:answer/id #uuid "66d51694-363d-5c40-816f-c4d01b887248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff8b912-fc25-51c6-abfb-2b5a13372f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717109} :answer-field/id #uuid "07f67a42-7370-5b54-8987-21bb4cfc90f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "393f076b-2648-5196-8ba9-aee4ad9df1e6" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{11}x&=\\cos\\theta \\\\ \ny&=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{11}y&=\\sin\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{121}x^2&=\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{121}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $\\frac{121}{4}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{121}x^2+\\frac{4}{121}y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{121}\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{121}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{11}{2}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d6d69df-a4af-5953-ac60-f722fdb1fe31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717112} {:answer/id #uuid "7f90c4da-301c-53db-886f-bb621afc23aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717114} {:answer/id #uuid "839f6618-da93-54d1-b7f9-2d020b157d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717117} {:answer/id #uuid "9947d7e6-a159-5471-a3ad-09a37b652602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717120} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd969d9-40bb-530c-becd-e5ffddfe5009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f90c4da-301c-53db-886f-bb621afc23aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717114} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed8aeef8-2bea-59c8-a1a0-0882b6d0fc02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6257a8d6-dadf-55d8-aa69-e9f5f970e209" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{1}{2}\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n2x&=\\cos\\theta \\\\ \ny&=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n2y&=\\sin\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x^2&=\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n4y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $\\frac{1}{4}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x^2+4y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n4\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49456d3d-d7ff-5664-b818-9614185aa266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717108} {:answer/id #uuid "aac63bf5-e11d-5f11-88ec-5028da719651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717122} {:answer/id #uuid "b358ebe0-dc13-5a56-8d7c-f2aafcc6c1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717123} {:answer/id #uuid "e14d83b1-893b-5545-bdeb-665ef7f09c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717125} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ffcc07-69ed-5373-9241-c1816dd90efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{16}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac63bf5-e11d-5f11-88ec-5028da719651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717122} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e7b1ad-d295-50df-a638-e5c65068e0c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85a850cb-806d-5604-b7fc-d47040dfc404" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{3}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{2}{3}\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{3}{2}x&=\\cos\\theta \\\\ \ny&=\\frac{2}{3}\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{3}{2}y&=\\sin\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{9}{4}x^2&=\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{9}{4}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $\\frac{4}{9}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{9}{4}x^2+\\frac{9}{4}y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{9}{4}\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{4}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{9}$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{2}{3}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65951512-6891-5cb1-bb98-1db483a38f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{49}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717168} {:answer/id #uuid "7c532591-f047-5324-a4fc-c618931adc1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{49}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717169} {:answer/id #uuid "bef5ba0d-c53a-56ea-a07d-c109973b616e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{4}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717176} {:answer/id #uuid "d086e0fd-5e95-50ce-b281-ec601a54d582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{49}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717177} {:ans