(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{7}{2}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278ac93d-2465-5aa8-bd07-4a9dc8d0897b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717159} {:answer/id #uuid "389ddf1e-3938-564d-b63b-d403361f78d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717161} {:answer/id #uuid "8c05b80a-9463-52cc-965f-972b50d268ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717172} {:answer/id #uuid "df483c16-d94f-59b4-b4f4-7a7e072ae609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717179} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ad0e53-729d-5488-a608-73890f94f508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "389ddf1e-3938-564d-b63b-d403361f78d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717161} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a232e43-6c71-589b-8803-bb82b481d175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6428cd64-a43e-5168-ab82-c4c5047c2d31" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{9}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{9}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nDividing each equation by $\\frac{9}{2}$ and squaring gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{81}x^2=\\cos^2\\theta,\\qquad \\frac{4}{81}y^2=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nUse $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$ to eliminate $\\theta$. Choose the Cartesian equation." :question/worked-solution "Undo any translations and divide by the common radius to isolate the trigonometric terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{9}{2}\\cos\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{9}x&=\\cos\\theta \\\\ \ny&=\\frac{9}{2}\\sin\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{2}{9}y&=\\sin\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both normalized equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{81}x^2&=\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{81}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$, then multiply by $\\frac{81}{4}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{81}x^2+\\frac{4}{81}y^2&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \n\\frac{4}{81}\\bigl(x^2+y^2\\bigr)&=1 \\\\ \nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{81}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}$. The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\frac{9}{2}$. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cf1e7e7-22bc-570e-a439-cd4ff7da3633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717163} {:answer/id #uuid "413dc327-c167-57d2-bd64-db6cdda6e12d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717164} {:answer/id #uuid "8205c496-86e5-5f1d-9e2f-b4183b052bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717170} {:answer/id #uuid "98ab11b7-2b4f-5bd1-8f31-b851ab6f274b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+y^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717173} {:answer/id #uuid "9dac4cb2-d35d-5205-ad43-1