b/ref 17592186717189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1b04aba-3cb0-5909-bbfb-4b42b38af8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1b04aba-3cb0-5909-bbfb-4b42b38af8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717207} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d21ba1-b5cd-57ee-834c-84ad68f0362a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd411712-c41f-5d6a-9b5d-9101ed19065e" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a964dd6d3033b513ab6d2e55d86453648dab39507fd49d477550ff9466443e55.png)\n\nThe solid arc is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta$? Use $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$ and include both filled endpoints.\n\n$\\theta\\in[$ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $]$" :question/worked-solution "The full circle has equations $x=h+r\\cos\\theta$, $y=k+r\\sin\\theta$, with $0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi$. Here the radius is $1$ and the center is $(0,0)$.\n\nThe parameter $\\theta$ measures the angle counterclockwise from the rightward horizontal ray through the center. The solid arc starts at $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ and ends at $\\theta=2\\pi$, following increasing angle. Both endpoints are included.\n\n![](images/6e/6e1d2c53ac21f3163f680337ff2753d7a0db9d38d57dedd0788d206f9f4f5772.png)\n\nTherefore the required restriction is $\\theta\\in[\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi]$. The parametric equations of the arc are\n\n$$\nx=\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=\\sin\\theta,\\qquad\\theta\\in[\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023f5a1d-e61f-5580-be7c-63f165c909d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717236} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8f7184-4b40-5b1d-b1ff-528adef8da28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717237} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea21d42-437b-51d2-8501-01aec4a84539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2\\pi]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717242} {:answer/id #uuid "6bcc35f8-eb7e-521c-8f7a-d95501995d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717243} {:answer/id #uuid "77846d30-8e0d-5f45-b4f9-65c105d93fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bcc35f8-eb7e-521c-8f7a-d95501995d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717243} :answer-field/id #uuid "522f0c1e-675d-5642-bb50-aa37ad9f1341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00385a70-fe74-5ba0-b0ca-2a913b00e95b" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b808ca263a43775db59b313adbfa7fe0a408d3ce2c9427ebfe509403edf29c8c.png)\n\nThe solid arc is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\cos\\theta+4,\\qquad y=\\sin\\theta+5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta$? Use $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$ and include both filled endpoints." :question/worked-solution "The full circle has equations $x=h+r\\cos\\theta$, $y=k+r\\sin\\theta$, with $0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi$. Here the radius is $1$ and the center is $(4,5)$.\n\nThe parameter $\\theta$ measures the angle counterclockwise from the rightward horizontal ray through the center. The solid arc starts at $\\theta=\\pi$ and ends at $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, following increasing angle. Both endpoints are included.\n\n![](images/92/9214153996ceb503d4ae6db6efcecabc0b241c13090080fe18f25878cad96216.png)\n\nTherefore the required restriction is $\\theta\\in[\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]$. The parametric equations of the arc are\n\n$$\nx=\\cos\\theta+4,\\qquad y=\\sin\\theta+5,\\qquad\\theta\\in[\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e32c1b5-8a50-5a2b-b941-63db3eee43f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717238} {:answer/id #uuid "32b4b395-d621-5edb-9668-dfd7d4bb0a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2\\pi]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717240} {:answer/id #uuid "85889c85-eb87-5a99-98f6-e4dcd444fd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717245} {:answer/id #uuid "d52b8436-157a-5093-8338-b4de347e5460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717246} {:answer/id #uuid "f04672b8-bb22-5350-b6ce-22a7ef28d2b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85889c85-eb87-5a99-98f6-e4dcd444fd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717245} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4a397ac-8482-56a7-87ec-031ed44c9ca3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "176ad5ff-a295-5a64-9e71-88c5020dd54d" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f90ce7ec0707632cfd8f0efffabfe4e9b8803f6ba6906b68b4f88117bb8e2339.png)\n\nThe solid arc is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=5\\cos\\theta-3,\\qquad y=5\\sin\\theta-1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta$? Use $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$ and include both filled endpoints." :question/worked-solution "The full circle has equations $x=h+r\\cos\\theta$, $y=k+r\\sin\\theta$, with $0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi$. Here the radius is $5$ and the center is $(-3,-1)$.\n\nThe parameter $\\theta$ measures the angle counterclockwise from the rightward horizontal ray through the center. The solid arc starts at $\\theta=0$ and ends at $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, following increasing angle. Both endpoints are included.\n\n![](images/ab/ab123b01039725c01cc87fc8ac0100066f1c5dca61c47815c1436c3cf9315b64.png)\n\nTherefore the required restriction is $\\theta\\in[0,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}]$. The parametric equations of the arc are\n\n$$\nx=5\\cos\\theta-3,\\qquad y=5\\sin\\theta-1,\\qquad\\theta\\in[0,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c7243c-272a-5dd2-a747-5f6f12bf19fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+t^4\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717971} {:answer/id #uuid "3f52bcb2-cf2c-5d0a-af36-ee64295aa36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(1+t^2\\sin t+t^4\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717975} {:answer/id #uuid "40c541ca-6e02-568a-94bd-3e0c543d7f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+2t^3\\sin t-t^4\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717976} {:answer/id #uuid "a357cfdd-6ec7-5578-9db1-1cb257bdaea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+2t^3\\sin t+t^4\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717981} {:answer/id #uuid "a6975387-359c-5ea5-a58d-40034f39ef8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+2t^3\\sin t+t^4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a357cfdd-6ec7-5578-9db1-1cb257bdaea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+2t^3\\sin t+t^4\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717981} :answer-field/id #uuid "38f52e6b-9c8f-5a41-ad8c-58dc6943e3d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fa19dc4-ab8a-5d2e-9cb5-90510b78a9b1" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=xe^{xy},$ $x=t^2,$ and $y=\\sin t,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}$ in terms of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths from f through x and y to t](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe two paths in the tree contribute products, which we add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}.\n$$\n\nThe partial derivative with respect to $x$ needs the product rule as well as the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{xy}+xy e^{xy}=(1+xy)e^{xy},\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x^2e^{xy}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=(1+t^2\\sin t)e^{t^2\\sin t},\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=t^4e^{t^2\\sin t}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=2t,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\cos t.\n$$\n\nBoth coordinate derivatives must multiply their corresponding partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=(1+t^2\\sin t)e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t)+t^4e^{t^2\\sin t}\\cos t\\\\\n&=e^{t^2\\sin t}(2t+2t^3\\sin t+t^4\\cos t).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51f65fa-ad63-589b-ad60-aff5acb409c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t(1+e^t)\\cos(t^2)-e^t\\sin(t^2)}{(1+e^t)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f51f65fa-ad63-589b-ad60-aff5acb409c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t(1+e^t)\\cos(t^2)-e^t\\sin(t^2)}{(1+e^t)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717986} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f3bead2-ab10-5181-a943-bb85364f3284" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c59d2341-8b2d-5e66-a539-265e20f0180d" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\dfrac{x}{1+y},$ $x=\\sin(t^2),$ and $y=e^t,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}$ in terms of $t.$\n\n$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths from f through x and y to t](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe two paths in the tree contribute products, which we add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to one intermediate variable at a time:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\frac{1}{1+y},\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-\\frac{x}{(1+y)^2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\sin(t^2)$ and $y=e^t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\frac{1}{1+e^t},\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-\\frac{\\sin(t^2)}{(1+e^t)^2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $x$ requires the inner derivative of $t^2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=2t\\cos(t^2),\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=e^t.\n$$\n\nMultiply along each path, then add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=\\frac{2t\\cos(t^2)}{1+e^t}-\\frac{e^t\\sin(t^2)}{(1+e^t)^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2t(1+e^t)\\cos(t^2)-e^t\\sin(t^2)}{(1+e^t)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two displayed forms are equivalent. Since $1+e^t>0,$ the derivative is defined for every real $t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a3fb293-a284-5299-bedb-7f04c8fdde82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos t-3t\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717970} {:answer/id #uuid "47960cdc-2641-5b6f-b8d4-265aed9115c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\cos t+t\\sin t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717977} {:answer/id #uuid "7c950ae6-e496-577a-a63d-aeae760feaf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717978} {:answer/id #uuid "957deabf-755e-5bc2-a8e0-6be27f3373b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sin t-t\\cos t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717980} {:answer/id #uuid "c627ca4d-9674-5ff4-9247-48e3f5e46324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\cos t-t\\sin t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c627ca4d-9674-5ff4-9247-48e3f5e46324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\cos t-t\\sin t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717984} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d224e76-f904-5e83-b6f4-5fb9287f5a85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf2d257a-1da7-5892-902e-c310b1e7040c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x\\cos y,$ $x=3t,$ and $y=t,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}$ in terms of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths from f through x and y to t](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe two paths in the tree contribute products, which we add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}.\n$$\n\nFirst find the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\cos y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=3t$ and $y=t$ into these expressions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\cos t,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-3t\\sin t.\n$$\n\nThe coordinate derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=3,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=1.\n$$\n\nMultiply along each path, then add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=(\\cos t)(3)+(-3t\\sin t)(1)\\\\\n&=3(\\cos t-t\\sin t).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718063 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "673b2a0a-4047-551d-957b-5603ad8b27ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718067} {:answer/id #uuid "741b23fd-037a-5f9f-ab0d-deaf9b5f2db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\cos x+x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718069} {:answer/id #uuid "89481cd4-e351-5a19-a8d8-1a4c4acb9298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\cos x-x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718070} {:answer/id #uuid "98785a7a-061e-54d4-811d-39ba84ad784b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\cos x-\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718071} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e1e393-4414-55f0-8cec-70c6f4208820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89481cd4-e351-5a19-a8d8-1a4c4acb9298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\cos x-x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718070} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61068d9-a421-5f37-96b1-597c8d4ac6e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05c75898-de56-5646-818e-300a5cb2dfe7" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^2+xy$ and $y=\\cos x$, compute $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is the independent variable and $y=y(x)$, the two contributions are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHolding the other variable fixed in each partial derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2x+y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=\\cos x$ into these expressions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2x+\\cos x,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin x.\n$$\n\nAdd the two chain-rule contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=(2x+\\cos x)+x(-\\sin x)\\\\&=2x+\\cos x-x\\sin x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first term accounts for the explicit dependence on $x$; the second accounts for the change through $y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b051064b-5577-5096-b481-69592f213a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x+x(x+1)\\cos x}{(x+1)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b051064b-5577-5096-b481-69592f213a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x+x(x+1)\\cos x}{(x+1)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718074} :answer-field/id #uuid "7335a7e3-3d28-53af-81bc-5f56574b52d0" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c0c248d-41ae-5a53-965c-5e213ee18fbf" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=\\dfrac{y}{x+1}$ and $y=x\\sin x$, where $x\\ne-1$. Compute the total derivative in terms of $x$.\n\n$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=$ {{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is the independent variable and $y=y(x)$, the two contributions are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHolding $y$ fixed when differentiating with respect to $x$, and $x$ fixed when differentiating with respect to $y$, gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=-\\frac{y}{(x+1)^2},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nAlong $y=x\\sin x$, these become\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=-\\frac{x\\sin x}{(x+1)^2},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nUse the product rule for the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\sin x+x\\cos x.\n$$\n\nCombine the two contributions over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-\\frac{x\\sin x}{(x+1)^2}+\\frac{\\sin x+x\\cos x}{x+1}\\\\&=\\frac{-x\\sin x+(x+1)(\\sin x+x\\cos x)}{(x+1)^2}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sin x+x(x+1)\\cos x}{(x+1)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is valid for $x\\ne-1$, as required by the original denominator."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cfe6cc7-06b7-5e82-9f9a-c48e59b6a747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718064} {:answer/id #uuid "23b2edcf-52f1-5dea-9211-035215eb9de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718065} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1caa17-7200-55c3-a867-48b2c335bced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2x\\sin x+x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718077} {:answer/id #uuid "dd81e9b6-e5b5-59ae-af88-69272f6ff0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+x\\sin x+x^2\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718078} {:answer/id #uuid "e66b934e-bf14-51fc-a1b1-beddab2ead1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2x\\sin x+x^2\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e66b934e-bf14-51fc-a1b1-beddab2ead1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2x\\sin x+x^2\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718079} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3045543-1336-5da7-af8e-2b9df7e5115b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9da553b0-5dba-547b-a7c9-cec905b54fd9" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^2+xy$ and $y=x\\sin x$, compute $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is the independent variable and $y=y(x)$, the two contributions are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHolding the other variable fixed gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2x+y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=x\\sin x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2x+x\\sin x,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x.\n$$\n\nThe dependency is a product, so both factors contribute to its derivative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=1\\cdot\\sin x+x\\cos x.\n$$\n\nNow apply the special-case chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=(2x+x\\sin x)+x(\\sin x+x\\cos x)\\\\&=2x+x\\sin x+x\\sin x+x^2\\cos x\\\\&=2x+2x\\sin x+x^2\\cos x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first term accounts for the explicit dependence on $x$; the second accounts for the change through $y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f1621f2-0d4d-5ded-a6a2-92c3bdc16659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^4t^2-4s^2t^3-4s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718084} {:answer/id #uuid "974aebe6-011d-50da-bcc8-457e6684ab72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s^4t^2-2s^2t^3+t^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718090} {:answer/id #uuid "b2680912-0b02-5895-99b1-ec1c76e8d830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5s^4t^2+6s^2t^3+t^4-4s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718094} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3ee940-d7c3-52fa-a22d-66f87e1c327e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5s^4t^2-6s^2t^3+t^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718096} {:answer/id #uuid "f265d602-6d46-54d2-8106-e6102169d255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5s^4t^2-6s^2t^3+t^4-4s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f265d602-6d46-54d2-8106-e6102169d255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5s^4t^2-6s^2t^3+t^4-4s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718100} :answer-field/id #uuid "efc90a79-d51d-5775-bb3d-978628729296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "952af84a-b9c4-559b-9d8c-e05372b13774" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=xy^2-2y$, where $x=st^2$ and $y=s^2-t$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to s](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply the derivatives along each highlighted path to $s$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=y^2,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2xy-2.\n$$\n\nWrite these derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=(s^2-t)^2,\\\\\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2st^2(s^2-t)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $s$, holding $t$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}=t^2,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}=2s.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=(s^2-t)^2t^2+\\bigl[2st^2(s^2-t)-2\\bigr](2s)\\\\&=(s^4t^2-2s^2t^3+t^4)+(4s^4t^2-4s^2t^3-4s)\\\\&=5s^4t^2-6s^2t^3+t^4-4s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "152a9d65-bced-5d15-a9fb-e12c87c74cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s^2(2t-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718081} {:answer/id #uuid "36ccc331-45ce-57c5-a8f6-d0f80dbcb601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6st" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718083} {:answer/id #uuid "4614b13e-a201-5af8-8904-a5599895da90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2st(t+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718085} {:answer/id #uuid "aaad7266-5f5c-5863-8381-5b3011e557a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2st(t-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718092} {:answer/id #uuid "f7778c02-60ad-5648-9a47-7b74f709e040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2st^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaad7266-5f5c-5863-8381-5b3011e557a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2st(t-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718092} :answer-field/id #uuid "736d225a-667b-531f-baa9-8355eec85456" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b73cbe4-d9c7-51e4-a22b-227209843674" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x^2-3y$, where $x=st$ and $y=s^2t$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to s](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply the derivatives along each highlighted path to $s$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2x,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-3.\n$$\n\nWrite these derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2st,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-3.\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $s$, holding $t$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}=t,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}=2st.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=(2st)(t)+(-3)(2st)\\\\&=2st^2-6st\\\\&=2st(t-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f23608b-204d-5e8e-b6f9-1c644b19af34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718082} {:answer/id #uuid "712a772b-a172-5a0f-a395-38c2742f66e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718086} {:answer/id #uuid "83c228ce-59f9-5bbe-abce-fa828c3ed000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718088} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a8d278-7853-5724-b2e4-08dd1bbfb416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718093} {:answer/id #uuid "e21ebce0-ebce-54ce-bcb6-63c989ec4b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1a8d278-7853-5724-b2e4-08dd1bbfb416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718093} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a7eed2-56e5-5bd1-93fa-a8fd6cb179a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bafb80bc-342c-5aa4-8af1-3109e90d38ca" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=2x-y$, where $x=s+3t$ and $y=2s-t$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to t](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply the derivatives along each highlighted path to $t$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-1.\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, holding $s$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}=3,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=(2)(3)+(-1)(-1)\\\\&=6+1\\\\&=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cba408d-7f1c-59d7-a632-147cd2d872bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718217} {:answer/id #uuid "606d15e4-9725-575a-9029-17d87973e13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718221} {:answer/id #uuid "62a475fb-2945-5152-af20-56342301cc3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718222} {:answer/id #uuid "948dca43-a722-53f2-8ebb-be8c7e44598c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718226} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8a7195-7426-5aa7-b8a0-e206ed888788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e8a7195-7426-5aa7-b8a0-e206ed888788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718228} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e78d18c-0eca-5854-baae-0bd83e061dda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "323759eb-2c94-5e02-8159-c168a205bb28" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=2x-y+z$, where $x=s+t$, $y=s-t$ and $z=2s+t$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. The highlighted paths ending at $t$ give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, differentiate the outer function with respect to its intermediate variables:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=-1,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, treating $s$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}=1,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}=-1,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}=1.\n$$\n\nMultiply along each path and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=2(1)+(-1)(-1)+1(1)\\\\\n&=2+1+1\\\\\n&=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a4ece37-0766-50ef-8664-63f23e173662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s^4t-3s^3\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718220} {:answer/id #uuid "8e79377f-d99a-5415-9503-ab9a46136872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^3t^2-6s^2\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718225} {:answer/id #uuid "9edad1d5-8ba4-52e0-ad09-9f2869b90f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s^3t^2-3s^2\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718229} {:answer/id #uuid "f17d95b1-5f0e-516d-a0ae-540f783e4495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^3t^2-9s^2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718235} {:answer/id #uuid "fc627b60-2168-51bb-95fb-162a9c9fd991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^3t^2-9s^2\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc627b60-2168-51bb-95fb-162a9c9fd991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^3t^2-9s^2\\sin t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718236} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae114e41-d9c0-54fc-8b7c-b6c41ffd8f84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b36b511e-e9e4-51d4-adb7-bc2bf7675222" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=x^2y-3yz$, where $x=st$, $y=s^2$ and $z=s\\sin t$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. The highlighted paths ending at $s$ give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}.\n$$\n\nFirst, take the outer partial derivatives while holding the other intermediate variables fixed:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=2xy,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x^2-3z,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=-3y.\n$$\n\nWrite these derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2(st)s^2=2s^3t,\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=s^2t^2-3s\\sin t,\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=-3s^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inner derivatives, with $t$ held fixed, are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}=t,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}=2s,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}=\\sin t.\n$$\n\nIn particular, $\\sin t$ is constant when differentiating with respect to $s$. Now multiply along all three paths:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=(2s^3t)t+(s^2t^2-3s\\sin t)(2s)+(-3s^2)\\sin t\\\\\n&=2s^3t^2+2s^3t^2-6s^2\\sin t-3s^2\\sin t\\\\\n&=4s^3t^2-9s^2\\sin t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth the $x$ and $y$ paths contribute to the polynomial term. Both the $y$ and $z$ paths contribute to the sine term."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b36e47-47ec-52ab-ad76-23ef2527c468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+2t+1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718216} {:answer/id #uuid "679547da-376f-598b-8f44-ff2e0117b940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+t-1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718224} {:answer/id #uuid "94d76a2e-98e7-5b47-8daf-f5f6bd78f01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2t-1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718227} {:answer/id #uuid "c623586f-c581-5011-bf96-ec2f835eb619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+t)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718232} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5e66ad-0436-5cc8-b8af-9144f1dc8120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+2t-1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5e66ad-0436-5cc8-b8af-9144f1dc8120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+2t-1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718233} :answer-field/id #uuid "6474060e-ed48-5bd2-acdb-1386ca012106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0e17ae9-e5cc-528f-b68f-dd625b31a953" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=e^{x+y+z}$, where $x=s-t$, $y=t^2$ and $z=st$. Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. The highlighted paths ending at $t$ give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}.\n$$\n\nThe three outer partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=e^{x+y+z},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=e^{x+y+z},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=e^{x+y+z}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the intermediate variables gives the common factor $e^{s-t+t^2+st}$. With $s$ held fixed, the inner partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}=-1,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}=2t,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}=s.\n$$\n\nSubstitute these into the chain rule and collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=e^{s-t+t^2+st}(-1)+e^{s-t+t^2+st}(2t)+e^{s-t+t^2+st}s\\\\\n&=(s+2t-1)e^{s-t+t^2+st}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
